{"description":"Planned 2026-10-07, next build after #696. The served root-cause skill gains a neighbours pass, used whenever the design names member designs (its pins with a graph_id) or the session reaches several designs:
- step 2 searches past causes in every member;
- a CHANGE-ACROSS bone uses upstream_status, or each member's changelog where it is hosted, to name the members that moved since this design last looked;
- a SEAM bone compares the interfaces this design uses or provides with the member's current version (mirrored interfaces, seam_report);
- a RIPPLE-BACK bone runs propagate_from with arriving_from from each member that moved, to see whether the change reaches the failing part;
- a member it cannot reach is named as not looked at.
The /hub skill separates where to LOOK (the whole family) from where to RECORD (the design where the cause lives, with the symptom's design linking to it). Mostly skill text, plus a test that both skills carry the steps. Compounding across designs (budgets and tolerances rolled up across the family) is NOT in this: req:a-quantity-that-compounds-across-designs-is-rolled-up-across-the-family, deferred.","distinct_from":["fact:a-root-cause-run-from-a-hub-investigates-one-design-and-the-hub-chooses-which-2026-10-07"],"name":"The root-cause skill walks a design's member designs (precedent, what moved, the seam, impact walked backwards), and the hub skill records the cause where it lives, not where it was asked","provenance":"authored","status":"realized"}
